  "text": "I'll start by reading the package, the test script, and the current failures so the fixes follow the documented behaviour.The tests fail because negative amounts are formatted with floor division, dates swap the month and day, and item ranking sorts the wrong way. I will fix those three causes.I fixed three bugs in `ledger/`. `python3 run_tests.py` now passes 6/6.\n\n- `format_cents` kept the minus sign inside the dollar amount. It now places the minus sign before `$`. `-310` formats as `-$3.10`. `-5` formats as `-$0.05`.\n- `parse_date` returned the day and the month in the wrong order. It now returns `(year, month, day)`.\n- `top_items` sorted the smallest totals first. It now sorts the largest total first. Equal totals sort by item name in ascending order.",
